  "Why people like to go to the entertaiment parks?": "People visit entertainment parks because they offer a perfect escape from everyday routine. There is adrenaline, laughter and games for every taste, which makes such parks great for both children and adults. On top of that, they create shared experiences and memories, because nothing brings friends closer than screaming together on a roller coaster.",





  "What are the pros and cons of roller-costers in parks?": "The pros are obvious, because roller coasters give an incredible adrenaline rush and are often the main reason people visit the park at all. The cons are equally real: long queues on busy days, some safety concerns, and of course, they are simply too scary for many visitors. So they divide people into two groups, fans and avoiders.",





  "Describe these images.": "Both images illustrate people doing the same everyday activity, but in two different generations, so to speak. In the first image, I can see that the activity is done traditionally, with people interacting in person and following the old routine. By contrast, the second image shows the same activity through modern technology, which makes it faster and more convenient. One similarity is that both images are about the same activity, so the viewer can compare them directly. However, the main difference is that the first image shows the classic, familiar way, whereas the second image highlights digitalisation and progress. Overall, I think the pictures demonstrate how our habits adapt to the times we live in.",





  "Why do people like to take pictures of themselves?": "I think it is a natural way of sharing our lives and expressing our identity. Taking photos of ourselves helps us capture good moments and boost our mood, especially with all the filters and effects. On a deeper level, it is simply human to want to be noticed, remembered and appreciated by others.",





  "Which one is easy taking selfies or taking photos with a camera?": "Taking a selfie is undeniably easier, you just stretch out your arm, tap the screen, and it is done within seconds. You can also retake it as many times as you like without asking anybody for help. A camera, on the other hand, requires more skill and settings, but it produces far better quality images.",





  "What can you observe in these two pictures?": "Both pictures illustrate people engaged in the same activity, but each one tells a different story. In the first picture, I can see that the activity is done in the traditional way, and people clearly value personal interaction. By contrast, the second picture shows the same activity being done with modern devices, which makes everything look quicker. One similarity is that both pictures are about the same everyday situation, so the comparison is straightforward. However, the main difference is that the first picture shows the old, familiar approach, whereas the second picture highlights how technology has made life easier. Overall, I would say the pictures remind us that while the activity stays the same, the way we do it keeps changing.",





  "What are the advantages of supermarkets?": "Supermarkets have several clear advantages. They offer a massive variety of goods under one single roof, from food to household items, which saves a lot of time. Prices are also clearly marked and often lower due to discounts, while everything is clean, well organised and convenient. That is why most families do their weekly shopping there.",





