  "What are advantages of studying offline?": "Studying offline gives you direct contact with teachers and classmates, which makes learning much more interactive. You can ask questions instantly, join discussions and get immediate feedback, and the structured routine helps you stay disciplined. Being physically present in a classroom also removes most distractions, so your attention stays on the lesson.",





  "What can you observe in these pictures?": "Both pictures illustrate people doing the same activity, but in clearly different styles. In the first picture, I can see that people do everything the traditional way, and the atmosphere is calm and personal. By contrast, the second picture shows the same activity in a modern setting, where technology takes the leading role. One similarity is that both pictures are about the same everyday activity, which makes the comparison easy to follow. However, the main difference is that the first picture shows the old-fashioned method, whereas the second picture highlights speed and convenience. Overall, I think the pictures are a perfect example of how the world around us is changing.",





  "How we can become healthy by doing fitness?": "Regular fitness is one of the most reliable roads to good health. It strengthens the heart, keeps your weight under control and boosts your energy and mood through endorphins. To get real results, you need consistency, a balanced diet and enough sleep, because fitness works best when it becomes a lifestyle rather than a short-term effort.",





  "Do you do any sporting activities?": "Yes, I try to stay active as much as possible. I play football with my friends at the weekend, and during the week I often go for a run. I am not a professional athlete by any means, but regular exercise helps me stay healthy, manage stress and keep my energy levels high throughout the day.",





  "What is your favorite animal?": "My favourite animal is the horse. In our culture, horses symbolise freedom and strength, which deeply appeals to me. I adore watching them run across the steppe, with their manes flying in the wind. One day, I would love to learn proper horse riding. Horses carry deep meaning in our culture, so this is a natural choice for me.",





  "What do you like to do at home?": "At home I usually read, watch series or listen to music on my headphones. I also chat with my family in the kitchen while someone is cooking. On free evenings, I like practising English with short podcasts. In short, my home is where I recharge after long days. Home is simply the place where I feel most myself.",





