  "Can you describe your family?": "There are four of us: my parents, my younger brother and me. My father works in construction, and my mother is a housewife with incredible cooking skills. My brother is still in school and keeps everyone entertained with his jokes. We are modest, but we get along very well. I know every family says this, but mine is truly special in my eyes.",





  "What types of books do you like to read?": "I am drawn to mystery and adventure books mainly, because they keep my attention from start to finish. I also enjoy self-development literature, when I want practical ideas for daily life. Occasionally I try classic fiction, though I find it heavier. Variety keeps my reading fresh. I trust my mood, honestly, when picking up the next book.",





  "Tell me about your room.": "My room is small but carefully organised. There is a desk by the window, a bookshelf with novels and study materials, and a soft carpet that makes it cosy. I decorated the wall with pictures from my travels. It reflects my personality, and I love spending time there. Friends say it is the cosiest room they have seen, which makes me proud.",





  "Do you like cooking?": "I like cooking, though I am still a beginner. I can prepare basic dishes like pasta, scrambled eggs and salads, and I enjoy experimenting with spices. Watching cooking videos inspires me to improve my skills. Honestly, the best reward is my family saying that the food tastes good. My personal goal is to master at least ten dishes before university ends.",





  "What is your favorite outdoor activity?": "My favourite outdoor activity is hiking in the mountains. There is nothing like reaching a hilltop and looking at the whole valley below, especially at sunset. The fresh air and silence completely reset my mind. I try to go hiking at least once a month when the weather allows. I honestly feel that every person needs a hobby like this one.",





  "What do you do at the weekends?": "At weekends I try to slow down and enjoy myself. I sleep a little longer, spend time with family, and meet friends when possible. Sometimes I go to the bazaar or take a short trip out of town. Overall, weekends are my time to recharge and reset. For me, weekends are a time to recharge, meet friends and prepare for the new week, and that balance keeps me happy.",





  "Who was your first teacher?": "My first teacher was a warm, patient woman named Mrs. Rakhimova. She taught us reading and writing, and she always made lessons feel like games. She would praise us for tiny successes, which built my confidence in class. I believe she is the reason I love learning languages today. Even today, I feel grateful whenever I remember her lessons.",





  "Where do you live?": "I live in the city centre, near the university. My flat is only a short walk from the main transport station, which is very handy for me. The neighbourhood is lively, with cafés and shops around, although it can be a bit noisy at night. Still, the location is perfect for a student. Everything I need is within walking distance, which saves me a lot of time.",





  "Do you like to get up early?": "Actually, I do, even though it is difficult at first. In the morning the city is quiet, and I get more done before noon, like studying or exercising. The trick is going to bed at a reasonable time. Once I manage that, mornings become my most productive hours. So yes, I genuinely prefer mornings once I am properly awake.",





  "What do you eat for breakfast?": "My typical breakfast is quite simple. I usually have bread with cheese and tea, sometimes with eggs or porridge. On weekends, I treat myself to pancakes or traditional pastries. I believe a solid breakfast is important, because it gives me energy for the morning lectures. Breakfast is honestly my favourite meal of the day. That small morning ritual sets the tone for my whole day.",





  "What is your favorite type of weather?": "My absolute favourite is a sunny spring day with a light breeze. The air is fresh, everything is blooming, and the temperature is perfect for walking or having tea outside. It feels like the whole world is renewing itself. Mood-wise, that weather makes me optimistic for the whole day. That kind of weather makes even ordinary days feel special.",





