  "Describe a rule that is important in your school or at work.": "Right, I would like to talk about a rule that is important in my life — at my university, there is a strict rule about mobile phones during lectures: students must keep their phones on silent and put them away completely, unless the lecturer asks us to use them for a task. Let me explain what the rule is about. It says that during lessons, phones are not allowed on the desks, so that everyone pays attention to the material and the lecturer is not interrupted. What happens when people break the rule? The consequences are quite clear. The first time, the student gets a verbal warning in front of the whole group, which is already embarrassing enough. If it happens again, the student may be asked to leave the classroom, and in serious cases, participation marks are reduced. Honestly, nobody wants to risk that, so the rule mostly works well. Why do I think it is an important rule? For several reasons. First of all, a lecture lasts less than two hours, and if even a few students scroll through their phones, the whole class loses focus and the lecturer has to repeat everything. Secondly, the rule teaches self-discipline, which is essential not only at university but also later in a real job. And finally, I have noticed that since this rule appeared, discussions in our group have become much livelier, because people actually listen to each other. So even though the rule feels annoying sometimes, I genuinely believe it makes our education much better, and I would even apply it to myself without hesitation.",





